# Test: a plugin walk faults one row and the operator sees both collections
#
# Flow:
# 1. A Go fixture writes a config declaring one external Go SDK plugin
# 2. The daemon starts, spawns `ze-test record-plugin`, and opens SSH
# 3. `ze cli -c "show test records fault | raw"` runs a walk of twelve rows
# 4. Row seven is wider than one wire message, so it has no line at all
# 5. The answer carries the eleven rows it applied and the one it refused
#
# A row wider than rpc.MaxMessageSize is rejected and the walk goes on
# (boundedRecord, pkg/plugin/rpc/answer_write.go), so refusing one row does not
# cost the operator the rows around it. The terminator states the two counts
# separately and positionally, the rows applied and then the rows refused, and
# a buffered reading of that answer is the two collections side by side: the
# handler's own envelope holds the applied rows and "errors" holds the refused
# one (CollapseRecords, pkg/plugin/rpc/collapse.go). Nothing lands in the
# applied collection that the terminator did not count, which is what keeps
# `| count` honest.
#
# This is the one payload whose two readings DIFFER, and that is what makes the
# test discriminate. A buffered rendering writes no line and rejects nothing, so
# a producer that built the whole answer would put the wide row in the document
# and lose the whole answer to the wire message ceiling.
#
# The rejected row names the record and states the two sizes. It quotes none of
# the row, because a fault carrying the row it rejected would be rejected for
# the same reason, and because a plugin's payload is not text an operator should
# meet inside an error.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-6 -- a row wider than one wire message is reported as a fault,
# the walk continues, and the terminator counts it under faults.
# VALIDATES: user story 3 -- an operator runs a plugin command that fails half
# way through its walk and sees the applied rows beside the rejected one.
# PREVENTS: one unwritable row costing the operator every row around it.


# Process orchestration
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/command-partial-fault:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: [0-9]+ rows applied and 1 rejected reached the operator together
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
